  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "App-defaults",
      "procedures": [
        "0x584fb4",
        "0x584e38",
        "0x5a8ac8",
        "0x5ce480",
        "0x430ce0"
      ],
      "claim": "The PE entry reaches the CRT routine that conditionally walks [5cfb58,5cfe38). Three actual pointer targets bind the independently decoded message initializers and App constructor view. App63c800 gets vptr5d6710 and explicit zero stores to +cc/+d0/+d4/+d8, then registers5ce480 for normal atexit cleanup. This proves selected source startup/default stores, not that startup or normal cleanup occurred in a running process.",
      "kind": "fact"
    },
    {
      "id": "message-identity",
      "procedures": [],
      "claim": "CRT entries401000/401020 register commctrl_DragListMsg and TaskbarCreated into63c7e0/63c7dc. Main registered-message rows bind41fe80/4238b0 respectively. They are drag-list/tray recreation messages, separate from App activation and the AAChannel reply adapter; no login generation identity follows from their registration.",
      "kind": "fact"
    },
    {
      "id": "ordinary-attempt",
      "procedures": [
        "0x41e420",
        "0x4291d0"
      ],
      "claim": "Ordinary submit initializes next candidate index main+1a7c from rand modulo count and remaining attempts+1a80 from count, sets busy+1a74 and stores the returned100ms timer in+1ff8. Each attempt decrements remaining, advances index modulo count, copies host/port into the Frame, stops the channel, clears request-sent+1a76, sets GetTickCount+10000 and starts the job in+1a78, recording its start result in+1a77. Failed starts immediately advance candidates. Neither+1a7c nor+1a80 is a request-generation field.",
      "kind": "fact"
    },
    {
      "id": "DNS-job-ownership",
      "procedures": [
        "0x418a10",
        "0x417aa0",
        "0x4260e0"
      ],
      "claim": "The job factory first clears/releases the output slot. Its shared counted admission allows at most4 outstanding counted resolver tasks. A normally allocated64-byte job starts with refs2/done0, owns a hostname string, a result buffer at+20, default status11001 at+38 and resolver pointer+3c. Successful thread creation closes its handle and publishes the job pointer; this does not join or stop the thread. Cap rejection and normal thread-start failure reduce the counter. Allocation-null and exceptional paths are not claimed fully handled.",
      "kind": "fact"
    },
    {
      "id": "DNS-worker",
      "procedures": [
        "0x426a30",
        "0x429fb0",
        "0x42a015",
        "0x4260e0"
      ],
      "claim": "The supplied426a30 function performs IPv4 stream getaddrinfo, uses the first result and formats an IPv4 address. The worker invokes that resolver with its owned host,job+20 and length22, stores status+38, then the normal cleanup publishes done atomically, reduces the counter and releases the worker reference. The selected normal worker route writes its private job, with no Main/window callback. Normal owner detachment therefore permits a late resolver to finish without publishing through an old Main-owned slot; it does not interrupt getaddrinfo.",
      "kind": "fact"
    },
    {
      "id": "timer-deadlines",
      "procedures": [
        "0x424cf0",
        "0x4291d0"
      ],
      "claim": "The DNS timer checks signed32(GetTickCount-deadline) before completion. At expiry it detaches/releases the current job and advances candidates. A completed job is copied locally, its status read, then detached/released and DNS phase cleared. Assembly restores decompiler-removed status0/nonempty-address checks and Connect(address,low16(port)). DNS resolution and channel readiness share the first10s deadline; an accepted login submission sets request-sent and starts another10s deadline. This is a source threshold, not measured wall-clock behavior.",
      "kind": "fact"
    },
    {
      "id": "stop-close-destroy",
      "procedures": [
        "0x41b690",
        "0x41a020",
        "0x42e260",
        "0x41fa60"
      ],
      "claim": "Stop clears/releases the current job, clears pending/request-sent/busy and remaining attempts, kills the stored timer or fallback100, and stops the channel. A pending close request is consumed and Frame WM_CLOSE posted. Frame close first defers through Main while busy; Main destruction also detaches/releases its job. These paths release owner references; no synchronous DNS termination follows from them.",
      "kind": "fact"
    },
    {
      "id": "reply-gate",
      "procedures": [
        "0x4316c0",
        "0x422b80",
        "0x422cb0",
        "0x423c30",
        "0x587340",
        "0x5875e0"
      ],
      "claim": "The reply adapter keeps the existing16-argument stack ABI proof and calls the success gate before the UI consumer. The gate requires Main busy and Stop returning no deferred close; otherwise it returnsfalse. The retry error helper also checks busy. Connect creates an internal channel and callback registration; Stop delegates internal teardown. The selected Main gates do not carry a candidate generation or prove that a reply from a superseded channel cannot reach a newly busy attempt. Full internal draining/dispatch ownership remains open.",
      "kind": "fact"
    },
    {
      "id": "separate-task-owners",
      "procedures": [],
      "claim": "Prior same-source contracts retain separate catalog task fields+2bc4/+2bc8, process busy handles+2b84/+2b88/+2b90, preparation/patch state and modal editing ownership. The DNS slot+1a78 and busy+1a74 do not replace these gates; inherited contracts and their remaining boundaries remain applicable.",
      "kind": "fact"
    }
  ],
  "scope_refinement": [
    "Same C82 source; older catalog/metadata source versions are not merged.",
    "CRT-derived views, canonical dossiers and retained-pseudocode compositions are separate.",
    "Selected normal job ownership is bound; the whole owner/exception/reentry graph is not closed."
  ],
  "inferences": [
    {
      "kind": "inference",
      "implementation_added": false,
      "claim": "D1 should keep candidate budget, owned resolver job, login busy/request phase, catalog work and process ownership separate. A shared attempt owner can preserve cancellation and selected deadline behavior while platform DNS/timer/channel adapters provide explicit late-event semantics. Any new generation token is an independent implementation mechanism, not a recovered wire field or proven native counter."
    }
  ],
